#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fail-closed summariser for the B1 answer-margin oracle K96 pilot.

Connects exactly three sources over the frozen 24-sample pilot manifest:

* ``dense``    - ``evaluation/results/cv_bench_l2_0875_full2638_20260916/shallow_r1000.jsonl``
* ``control``  - ``artifacts/token_selector/2026-10-04-b1-corrected-l2-prompt-ablation-full2638/corrected_l2_integer_k96_full2638.jsonl``
* ``oracle``   - the new B1 answer-margin oracle raw JSONL (generated by the GPU
  runner; missing -> fail closed, no report written).

Official scoring only: :func:`evaluation.build_cv_bench_pruning_report.parse_choice`
and :func:`~evaluation.build_cv_bench_pruning_report.score`.  Reported values are
the three absolute accuracies, the dense headroom, the oracle-minus-control
W->R / R->W / net transitions, parse rates, and (diagnostic only) selected-set
overlap / Jaccard and oracle saliency retained mass.

The pre-registered pilot gate is ``oracle - control net >= 3``, ``W->R >= 4``,
``R->W <= 1``, ``oracle parse >= 23/24`` and all 24 exact K96 layout contracts
pass -> ``PILOT_GO``; otherwise ``PILOT_STOP``.

Hard rules
----------
* This is a **label-aware oracle** with ground-truth answer leakage over 24
  samples.  It is not deployable, not paper accuracy and **no confidence
  interval** is computed; no "accuracy improvement confirmed" wording is used.
* Every pin, id set, ``arm`` / budget / grid / layout / record hash is checked
  before any score; any failure raises :class:`InputContractError` and the
  formal report is not written.
"""

